    "field_name": "Raw Output Format",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "raw_results.csv, raw_results.jsonl, and gemm plus conv2d text in raw_output.txt. collect_workload.py copies raw_results.csv to the harness raw file"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Primary Record Granularity",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "three CSV rows (gemm, conv2d, summary) carrying the same six values"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Raw Output Example",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "check,device_id,dtype,kernel_type,status,gemm_time_usec,gemm_tflops,gemm_bandwidth_gb_s,conv_time_usec,conv_tflops,conv_bandwidth_gb_s\nsummary,0,fp16,all,ok,20,10,400,30,8,300"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Smoke Run",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --smoke --validate --device-id 0 --kernel-type all --dtype fp16 --input-shape 1,3,32,32 --M 64 --N 64 --K 64 --batch-size 1 --warmup-iters 2 --num-iterations 5 --seed 42"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Baseline Run",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --baseline --validate --device-id 0 --kernel-type all --dtype fp16 --input-shape 1,3,224,224 --M 4096 --N 4096 --K 4096 --batch-size 8 --warmup-iters 10 --num-iterations 800000 --seed 42"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "run_benchmark Command Plus Options for Extended Run",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "bash run_benchmark.sh --extended --validate --device-id 0 --kernel-type all --dtype fp16 --input-shape 8,3,224,224 --M 4096 --N 4096 --K 4096 --batch-size 8 --warmup-iters 20 --num-iterations 1800000 --seed 42"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Output Fields / Metrics to Parse",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "gemm_time_usec, gemm_tflops, gemm_bandwidth_gb_s, conv_time_usec, conv_tflops, conv_bandwidth_gb_s"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Success Criteria",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "gemm.py and conv2d.py exit 0 and print all six values, and every value is positive"
  },
  {
    "field_name": "Parser and Normalization Notes",
    "source_file": "BenchmarkSpecDefinitions.xlsx::Workload_Definitions",
    "value": "GEMM and Conv2d are separate metrics; nothing is averaged across kernels. Conv2d FLOPs are 2 x N x Cout x H x W x Cin x 9 (Cout = 8) and its bytes count input, weights, and output. A failed script or missing value fails the run (no 1.0 default). The three rows carry the same values"
  },
